Message-ID: <8uhun-sKeC8.aw_wjyETYGwJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <8uhun-sKeC8.b3ek_QOoqj0J@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <8uhun-sKeC8.b3ek_QOoqj0J@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/8uhun-sKeC8/m/aw_wjyETYGwJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Code them as AA/BB, and include a phenotype "sex", with all 1's.
(or M's).  And make sure that you call the chromosomes "X".

If the genotypes are being called AA/AB in the software,
ignore that.  Or maybe check that you are using the latest version.
I thought that was now fixed.

karl

